    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW28CHnH1Ew1Kqrdet3ZGPrWT)_\n\n## What\n\nNew module `sp-see-also` (academic): reads the \"see also\" reminders I leave in litnotes as inline footnotes, `[fn::[[id:...][Concept]]]`, and ranks them. Literate doc: `docs/tangles/academic/sp-see-also.org`.\n\n- **Scanner** (`sp-see-also-parse-buffer`): finds inline footnotes with an `id:` link and records the context of each: `quote` or `prose`, and the open question heading above it (keywords come from `sp-org-keywords-research`, so `QUESTION SCOPING READING SYNTHESIZING REVIEW` are open; `STABLE ANSWERED DROPPED` are closed).\n- **No buffers visited**: files are read with `insert-file-contents` into a temp buffer in `fundamental-mode` (no hooks, no `org-mode`, no `org-element`). A test checks its footnote ranges against `org-element`. Unsaved open buffers are read from the buffer.\n- **Cache**: per file, keyed by mtime and size, kept in `var/cache/see-also-index.eld`; reset when the keywords change. Vulpea gives the litnote list, the titles, and (via `vulpea-db-query-links-to`) the files that link to a concept, so a concept lookup reads only those. The whole-vault index is the fallback.\n- **Priority**: two replaceable functions, `sp-see-also-concept-score-function` and `sp-see-also-question-priority-function`. Default: mention weight (prose 1, quote 2, plus the keyword weight when under an open question), times `1 + ln(1 + other litnotes)`.\n- **Dashboards**: a `see-also` vulpea-ui widget (concepts by score, then open questions) and a `concept-usage` widget plus `#+BEGIN: concept-usage` dynamic block (litnote, where, under, context).\n\n## Measured\n\nSynthetic vault of 300 files (about 100 KB each), Emacs 29.3 batch: cold 0.65 s, warm from the disk cache 0.02 s.\n\n## Tested\n\n17 ERT tests (`tests/sp-see-also-test.el`, all pass): context classification, org-element agreement, cache hit/miss/keyword reset, unsaved buffers, no buffer left behind, scoring, hook replacement, dblock output.\n\n## Not tested\n\n- The vulpea-ui widgets (no `vui` in the cloud container; the file only reads cleanly) and the real `vulpea-db-query-links-to` shape.\n- Anything against the real vault.\n- The original \"General academic system\" conversation could not be opened from this project, so the design is built from the request.\n\n## Notes for the sidenote PR\n\n`sp-see-also-parse-buffer` is the shared footnote parser (`:beg :end :label :text :links` plus context). `sp-reading-mode` / ox-tufte should call it rather than parse footnotes again.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edits (nightly tidy owns them).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiB1kXTza1J2p1MBw5q)_",
